\title{Ownership can be acquired speculatively}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786316438961}

\prompt{When is the [[GA7N]] request for a store actually issued in a real core, and why is that safe?}{
  Usually at \strong{AGU execute time}, as soon as the physical address is known — a real Upgrade/GetM on the fabric, tens of cycles before retirement. This is why store misses often look free in traces: the latency was paid during [[IIF9]], not at drain.

  It is safe because ownership is \strong{architecturally invisible}. If the store is squashed, or the line is snooped away before the merge, nothing is lost but fabric traffic.
}
